## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzles
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-02-15
Number: 9
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a shaded cross in the centre printed "No 9" (shown as _), and two words printed in the grid as a starter: FUN (r2c6-c8) and PUZZLES (r4c4-c10); clues name four words by those printed letters (F-4, P-23, N-5, S-24). The number is printed in the centre block ("No 9") and in the intro ("the ninth in FUN'S series"). No credit line is printed. Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_02_15_83.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_02_22_83.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.
Numbering: across-first


